foundation.question_text:
The electricity meter readings for a residential property are shown below.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\small},
  cell/.style={draw, minimum height=0.65cm, inner xsep=5pt, anchor=west},
  hdr/.style={cell, fill=gray!25, font=\small\bfseries}]
\def\colA{3.2cm} \def\colB{2.2cm} \def\colC{2.6cm}
\node[hdr, minimum width=\colA] (h1) at (0,0) {Meter Reading};
\node[hdr, minimum width=\colB, right=0pt of h1] (h2) {Value};
\node[hdr, minimum width=\colC, right=0pt of h2] (h3) {Units};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colA, below=0pt of h1.south west, anchor=north west] (a1) {Current Reading};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colB, right=0pt of a1] (a2) {52 480};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colC, right=0pt of a2] (a3) {kWh};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colA, below=0pt of a1.south west, anchor=north west] (b1) {Previous Reading};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colB, right=0pt of b1] (b2) {50 860};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colC, right=0pt of b2] (b3) {kWh};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Calculate the total electricity consumed in $\text{kWh}$.

An extract from a quarterly water bill is shown below.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\small},
  cell/.style={draw, minimum height=0.65cm, inner xsep=5pt, anchor=west},
  hdr/.style={cell, fill=gray!25, font=\small\bfseries}]
\def\colA{4.4cm} \def\colB{2.6cm}
\node[hdr, minimum width=\colA] (h1) at (0,0) {Charge Description};
\node[hdr, minimum width=\colB, right=0pt of h1] (h2) {Amount (\$)};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colA, below=0pt of h1.south west, anchor=north west] (a1) {Water Usage (54 kL @ \$2.40/kL)};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colB, right=0pt of a1] (a2) {\$129.60};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colA, below=0pt of a1.south west, anchor=north west] (b1) {Water Service Charge};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colB, right=0pt of b1] (b2) {\$45.00};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colA, below=0pt of b1.south west, anchor=north west] (c1) {Sewerage Service Charge};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colB, right=0pt of c1] (c2) {\$160.00};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Water and sewerage charges are GST-free.
Calculate the total current charges for this water account.

development.question_text:
An electricity account charges time-of-use rates as shown below.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\small},
  cell/.style={draw, minimum height=0.65cm, inner xsep=5pt, anchor=west},
  hdr/.style={cell, fill=gray!25, font=\small\bfseries}]
\def\colA{3.4cm} \def\colB{1.8cm} \def\colC{2.4cm}
\node[hdr, minimum width=\colA] (h1) at (0,0) {Tariff Component};
\node[hdr, minimum width=\colB, right=0pt of h1] (h2) {Usage};
\node[hdr, minimum width=\colC, right=0pt of h2] (h3) {Rate (ex GST)};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colA, below=0pt of h1.south west, anchor=north west] (a1) {Peak Electricity};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colB, right=0pt of a1] (a2) {850 kWh};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colC, right=0pt of a2] (a3) {34.5 c/kWh};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colA, below=0pt of a1.south west, anchor=north west] (b1) {Off-Peak Electricity};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colB, right=0pt of b1] (b2) {1200 kWh};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colC, right=0pt of b2] (b3) {16.0 c/kWh};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colA, below=0pt of b1.south west, anchor=north west] (c1) {Daily Supply Charge};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colB, right=0pt of c1] (c2) {92 days};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colC, right=0pt of c2] (c3) {\$1.05/day};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Calculate the total electricity account including $10\%$ GST, rounded to the nearest cent.

A gas provider bills customers using a step tariff as shown below.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\small},
  cell/.style={draw, minimum height=0.65cm, inner xsep=5pt, anchor=west},
  hdr/.style={cell, fill=gray!25, font=\small\bfseries}]
\def\colA{3.4cm} \def\colB{2.2cm} \def\colC{2.4cm}
\node[hdr, minimum width=\colA] (h1) at (0,0) {Step Tariff};
\node[hdr, minimum width=\colB, right=0pt of h1] (h2) {Threshold};
\node[hdr, minimum width=\colC, right=0pt of h2] (h3) {Rate (ex GST)};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colA, below=0pt of h1.south west, anchor=north west] (a1) {Step 1};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colB, right=0pt of a1] (a2) {First 3000 MJ};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colC, right=0pt of a2] (a3) {3.8 c/MJ};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colA, below=0pt of a1.south west, anchor=north west] (b1) {Step 2};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colB, right=0pt of b1] (b2) {Over 3000 MJ};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colC, right=0pt of b2] (b3) {2.9 c/MJ};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colA, below=0pt of b1.south west, anchor=north west] (c1) {Supply Charge};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colB, right=0pt of c1] (c2) {62 days};
\node[cell, minimum width=\colC, right=0pt of c2] (c3) {\$0.95/day};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A customer consumes $5500\text{ MJ}$ over $62$ days.
Calculate the total gas invoice including $10\%$ GST.
